  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Add a contributor-facing machine onboarding checklist covering sourced facts, units/coordinates, axis and spindle limits, controller/post fit, and manual citation/redistribution boundaries.\r\n- Point to the actual `.mch` parser/checker/mirror, machine and post registries, and existing test seams rather than inventing a new configuration API.\r\n- Provide a milling/turning operation and fixture matrix plus seven reproducible existing-test commands. Reuse `Milling-test.step` and the original synthetic turning fixtures; distinguish missing knurl and end-to-end lathe-tapping coverage.\r\n- Document current JSON-comment, unknown rigid-tapping, and headless-interface limits. MCP can verify machine data in an opened project, but has no direct `.mch` loader.\r\n- Keep physical-machine acceptance separate: software fixtures are not machine certification. No machine, post dialect, UI, schema, verifier, dependency or toolpath change.\r\n\r\nReadings: `AGENTS.md`, `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`, `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`, the current machine/post/MCP/project source and the linked existing tests. Decisions are in `docs/decisions/298-machine-onboarding.md`.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nSeven selected Windows tests executed successfully, each with native exit 0 and one passing test:\r\n\r\n- `machine::every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration`\r\n- `posting::machine_limits_block_the_post_and_within_limits_does_not`\r\n- `tormach_machines::every_tormach_machine_states_its_manuals_figures`\r\n- `tormach_machines::a_tap_job_posts_on_the_1100mx_and_is_refused_on_the_770m`\r\n- `lathe_post::an_axial_drill_posts_through_the_document_with_the_lathe_post_chosen`\r\n- `lathe_post_g76::a_g76_thread_posts_to_the_lathe_golden`\r\n- `lead_approach::every_lead_option_on_the_users_part_verifies_silent` (imports the existing STEP model)\r\n\r\nThese ran on `205eeaa4b0c09035193f4f569a881d0ce9fe5285`; the final commit changes only one documentation paragraph and adds the already-exercised STEP command. Runtime inputs are unchanged, so those results are reused, not represented as a new run.\r\n\r\nOn final head `7127a273ec990d570cc673309af0c51c96cc098d`, `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base 51b80a5d362dc0b2bcf8a4592fb8a8dfa427c35a` exited 0. Its docs-only mapping selected **zero Rust steps**; this is not additional runtime-test evidence. Local link/line-target and exact-test-name checks passed (36 links, seven targets); `git diff --check` passed. Independent static technical/documentation review passed after correcting the MCP wording.\r\n\r\n## Limits\r\n\r\nNo new all-operations qualification job is introduced. The guide explains which existing fixtures are useful and what remains unsupported/unverified. No real machine execution, NC transfer, physical acceptance, Linux/macOS run, full/release campaign or hosted workflow dispatch was performed. Hosted checks are intentionally absent under the repository's local-gate workflow policy, not reported as green CI. Maintainer review/merge remains manual.\r\n\r\nChangelog: none (documentation only).\r\n\r\nFixes #298\r\n",
